Identity and Access Management (IAM)

IAM focuses on controlling access and authorization to keep data secure by ensuring users follow established policies.
Its goal is to reduce overall risk to systems and data by limiting user access to only what is necessary for their roles.
Security Assessment and Testing

This domain involves conducting security control testing, collecting and analyzing data, and performing security audits to monitor for risks, threats, and vulnerabilities.
Regular assessment helps identify new ways to mitigate threats and improve existing controls, such as implementing multi-factor authentication.
Security Operations

Security operations concentrate on conducting investigations and implementing preventative measures after a security incident has been identified.
This includes mitigating active attacks, conducting forensic investigations to understand the breach, and determining preventative measures for future attacks.
Software Development Security

This domain emphasizes using secure coding practices and integrating security throughout the software development lifecycle.
Security reviews at each phase, such as secure design reviews, code reviews, and penetration testing, ensure security is embedded into the software product from the start.
